<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Rakshasbhuvan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1763">1763</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Rakshasbhuvan was fought in August 1763 on the Godavari between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a> under the young <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peshwa">Peshwa</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhavrao-i">Madhavrao I</a> and the army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizam-ali-khan">Nizam Ali Khan</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyderabad">Hyderabad</a>. The Nizam had tried to exploit Maratha losses at Panipat in 1761, but his defeat restored Maratha power in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a>.</p></div>
